1212	\subsection{Commuting EPR strategies}
1213	
1214	In this section, we introduce a class of strategies important for our proof.
1215	
1216	\begin{definition}
1217	A strategy $\calS = (\psi, M)$ is called an \emph{EPR strategy} if it satisfies the following two properties.
1218	First, there is an integer~$k$ and powers of two $q_1, \ldots, q_k$ such that
1219	\begin{equation*}
1220	\ket{\psi} = \ket{\mathrm{EPR}_{q_1}} \otimes \ket{\mathrm{EPR}_{q_2}} \otimes \cdots \otimes \ket{\mathrm{EPR}_{q_k}}.
1221	\end{equation*}
1222	Second, for each question~$x$, $M^x$ is a projective measurement. If
1223	for all questions $x$ and answers $a$, $M^x_a$ is a real-valued
1224	matrix, we say that the strategy is \emph{real}
1225	
1226	In addition, given a game~$\game$, we say that a real EPR strategy $\calS$ is a \emph{real
1227	  commuting EPR strategy (with respect to~$\game$)}
1228	if for every~$(x_1, x_2)$ in the support of~$\calS$ and every~$a_1, a_2$, $M^{x_1}_{a_1}$ commutes with $M^{x_2}_{a_2}$.
1229	We denote the set of real commuting EPR strategies by $\comstrat{\game}$.
1230	\end{definition}
1231	
1232	Real commuting EPR strategies are motivated by the \emph{completeness} cases that arise in this work.
1233	We give a series of transformations which modify games to make them sound against increasingly broader sets of strategies.
1234	Unfortunately, these transformations are not complete for all strategies, in the sense that value-$1$ strategies may be mapped to value-less-than-1 strategies,
1235	but we will be careful to ensure that they \emph{are} complete for all commuting EPR strategies.
1236	For the majority of the paper, the one property of commuting EPR strategies that we will use, not shared by all value-$1$ strategies, is the following.
1237	
1238	\begin{fact}\label{fact:heh-heh-heh-gonna-make-anand-prove-this-so-i-can-take-the-day-off}
1239	Let $(\psi, M)$ be a real EPR strategy.
1240	Then $M^x_a \otimes I_{\reg{Bob}} \consistency_0 I_{\reg{Alice}} \otimes M^x_a$ for every distribution on~$x$.
1241	\end{fact}
1242	\begin{proof}
1243	  From the definition of EPR strategies, we know that $\ket{\psi} =
